-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Kimble County record runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, across 8 grids. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, January to February came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, and May to June is the wettest pair at 6.19 inches normal. In 2025 the middle got 27% of normal in February to March and 236% in June to July. Grid 12720 had its driest year in 1951 at 38%.</p>"}
